Third-party components and data

1. Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M-TL (IBM and NASA), Apache License 2.0 (Szwarcman et al. 2025, arXiv:2412.02732).
   The Prithvi-OpenET weights (prithvi_openet_opt*) do not include the encoder: it is used unchanged and is downloaded
   from Hugging Face (ibm-nasa-geospatial/Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M-TL, revision 63adbd39c271da4c42f447e69b1a7c91a338cdc9)
   under its own Apache License 2.0. The Prithvi-OpenET-Tower weights (prithvi_openet_tower_*) include an encoder
   derived from Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M-TL by fine-tuning on flux-tower observations.

2. Copernicus DEM GLO-30. Elevation and clear-sky shortwave radiation in the example
   chips were produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus
   Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and
   ESA; all rights reserved. The organisations in charge of the Copernicus programme by
   law or by delegation do not incur any liability for any use of the Copernicus
   WorldDEM-30.

3. MERIT Hydro v1.0.1 (Yamazaki et al. 2019), CC BY-NC 4.0. The topographic wetness index
   input of the Opt.+F+E models derives from MERIT Hydro; for this reason the model weights
   (all six models, for consistent terms) and the example chips are released for
   non-commercial use.

4. OpenET Collection v2.1 (Earth Engine assets, CC BY 4.0). The models were trained on these
   labels; the labels themselves are not redistributed.

5. FLUXNET-1F data (CC BY 4.0), obtained with the FLUXNET Shuttle, were used to adapt the Prithvi-OpenET-Tower models.
